From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yvan Janssens <yvanj@cyber.gent>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:47:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] s390x: build with a fixed build user and host name

The kernel puts the account and the machine it was built on into its
version banner. Set KBUILD_BUILD_USER and KBUILD_BUILD_HOST for s390x
builds, so that the packages do not depend on where they were built.
The time stamp already comes from the changelog.
---
 debian/rules.d/s390x.mk | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/debian/rules.d/s390x.mk b/debian/rules.d/s390x.mk
index 62594a76546f..ea19aec545a8 100644
--- a/debian/rules.d/s390x.mk
+++ b/debian/rules.d/s390x.mk
@@ -9,3 +9,7 @@ GRUB_RECOMMENDS     = s390-tools
 FIRMWARE_DEPENDS    =
 # the Rust toolchain is not a build dependency on this architecture
 NEED_RUST           = no
+# the kernel records who built it where (version banner, /proc/version): use
+# a fixed identity instead of the build account and machine name
+export KBUILD_BUILD_USER := build
+export KBUILD_BUILD_HOST := proxmox-390
